{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall be cleared of this oath.</b> 'This' implies a restriction, to say that from the oath of ״כי אל ארצי ואל מולדתי תלך״ you shall be cleared, but from the oath of ״לא תקח אשה לבני״ you shall not be cleared. According to this, it must be that Eshkol and Mamre were not Canaanites." "<b>Only do not bring my son back there.</b> Even though he had never been there, the language of 'returning' applies also to Isaac, on account of Eliezer who was going with him — and for him it would be an actual returning, for he had already been there. And likewise with Ruth the Moabitess: ״השבה עם נעמי משדי מואב״, and even though Ruth had never been there, he calls it in the language of 'returning' on account of Naomi who was going with her."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The name Anner (ענר) appears absent from the first item in the list; translated as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:53.598225961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}